&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-indent:.5in'>&lt;span
style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman",serif'>            When
the Christian gospel came on the scene of redemptive history, the status and
nature of the Mosaic Law came under question. Not only was that question
relevant to the Jews, but the Gentiles also had to cope with it because
Christianity came out of a heritage different from their own. Christendom has demonstrated
five ways of dealing with the issue.&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>NOTATIONS ON THE DOCUMENTARY THEORY FOR ORIGINS OF THE PENTATEUCH</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/evidences/critical-intro-ot/notations-on-the-documentary-theory-for-origins-of-the-pentateuch/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/evidences/critical-intro-ot/notations-on-the-documentary-theory-for-origins-of-the-pentateuch/</guid><description>&lt;style>
